{"path": "SECURITY_REVIEW.json", "content": "{
  "findings": [
    {
      "category": "missing-authentication",
      "severity": "CRITICAL",
      "files": ["src/routes.js"],
      "evidence": "getInvoice(req, res) calls invoices.findById(req.params.id) and returns res.json(invoice) without ever inspecting req.user. A repository-wide grep shows the only req.user check in the codebase is in src/admin.js (req.user.role === 'admin'); the public invoice route has no authentication guard at all. Consequently any unauthenticated request can retrieve any invoice by supplying an id, e.g. GET /invoices/<id> returns the full record with no credential required. This is distinct from per-object ownership: the request is never tied to an identity in the first place.",
      "remediation": "Require authentication on the invoice route: add an auth middleware that populates and validates req.user (rejecting with 401 when req.user is absent) before performing the lookup, mirroring the guard pattern already present in src/admin.js."
    },
    {
      "category": "insecure-direct-object-reference",
      "severity": "HIGH",
      "files": ["src/invoices.js", "src/routes.js"],
      "evidence": "The shared data-access layer invoices.findById(id) executes 'select * from invoices where id = ?' with no user_id/owner predicate, and getInvoice returns the result without comparing the invoice's owner to req.user.id. Even after adding authentication, any authenticated user could enumerate invoice ids via req.params.id and read invoices belonging to other users (Broken Object Level Authorization / IDOR). The authorization gap lives in both layers: the query is not scoped by owner and the route never verifies ownership of the returned object.",
      "remediation": "Scope the query by owner, e.g. 'select * from invoices where id = ? and user_id = ?' passing req.user.id, and/or in getInvoice verify the returned invoice.user_id === req.user.id and respond 403/404 on mismatch. Centralize this in findById so all callers of the shared data-access code inherit the ownership constraint."
    }
  ],
  "scanned_files": ["src/invoices.js", "src/routes.js", "src/admin.js"],
  "source_modified": false
}
"}

